hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"926","It is narrated by Ahmad bin Abdah, it is Abd al-Ala, it is Saeed, meaning Ibn Iyas al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw phlegm in the direction of the mosque, so he cleaned it out by taking a stick with him, then he turned to the people. They would know. Anger appeared on his face, so he said: “Which of you is the owner of this phlegm?” They remained silent, so he said: “Would any of you like, when he stood up to pray, for a man to meet him and sneeze in his face?” They said: No. He said: “For God Almighty is before you in your prayers, so do not direct any harm in front of you, but rather at the left of one of you or under his feet\""
"
